 "notes_text": "A bell tower. A G5 bell rings on beats 1 and 3 ('ding-dong-ding') while the inner voice sinks Eb-D-C and the bass walks down the lament tetrachord C-Bb-Ab-G, so the same G changes colour underneath (fifth of i, added sixth over VII, major seventh over VI, root of V): eerie stillness over a falling floor. The 'a u a' contour keeps the original's quarter-note pulse, fused top voice and narrow register (B4-Ab5, 9 semitones, 92 % in C5-G5) but turns its rising u-a-a inside out. Spins: a rising lift B-C-D into V7 (bar 4), a two-beat swirl C-D-Eb | F-Eb-F climbing back to the bell (bar 6), a turn on the 'u' (bar 8). The cry is the bell cracking: at 7.9 s it rises a semitone to Ab5, the b9 over V7(b9), and falls straight back to G on the next beat (approached by step, not by a leap). Cadence: iv with added sixth (D against Ab) to V7, the tonic an eighth early, held over the waltz; V6/5 under it at the end for the loop."
